    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d328-a10">

                <pb facs="0771" n="675" sameAs="frus:frus1879/pg675"/>

                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1879-07-10"><hi rendition="#small-caps">July</hi> 10,
                        1879</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p rendition="#flush">To <hi rendition="#small-caps">E. Zappe</hi>, Esq.,<lb/><hi
                        rendition="#italic">His Imperial German Majesty’s Consul:</hi></p>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge the receipt
                    of your dispatch dated the 8th instant. The various points with regard to the
                    examination of German vessels, as mentioned in your dispatch of the 4th instant,
                    have not by any means been cast aside.</p>
                <p>I have received information by telegram that the German steamer “Hesperia”
                    weighed anchor from the port of Kobe at 10 p.m. yesterday; and I shall
                    accordingly cause the inspecting officers to carry with them the document sent
                    by you, and measures shall be taken in the sea off Yokoska, according to the
                    regulations mentioned in your letter. I beg you, therefore, to take note of the
                    above.</p>
                <p>I have, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>NOMURA YASUSHI</signed>, [<hi rendition="#small-caps">l.
                        s.</hi>]<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Ken Rei of Kanagawa.</hi></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
